  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1141 PM CDT MON OCT 26 2026\n\nDry conditions are expected to remain for most of the upcoming\nweek, as upper-level ridging stays in place through Wednesday. By\nThursday, the ridge will finally break down and shift to the east,\nas a deep trough sets up to the west. This will put the region\nback into SW flow aloft, allowing for slow moisture return into\nthe weekend. During this timeframe, temperatures will climb ever\nso slightly, settling into the upper-70s and low 80s. \n\nBy Friday morning, it appears as if a weak closed low pressure\nwill develop along the TX/NM border, before moving NE into the\ncentral Plains. During this time, a shortwave will branch off this\nclosed low, working away from the apex to the east, riding the SW\nflow aloft. This shortwave should begin to affect the region by\nSaturday afternoon in the form of increased rain probabilities. As\nthis closed low continues to work to the NE through the weekend,\nas will the rainfall, with rain staying in the forecast through\nSunday afternoon. While total rainfall amounts remain to be seen,\nany rainfall will be a sight for sore eyes. \n\n/44/",
